@startuml LLM_Lifecycle
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #E8F5E9
  BorderColor #388E3C
  FontSize 12
  FontColor #263238
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
  DiamondBorderColor #F57F17
}

title End-to-End LLM Lifecycle (Text-Token-Embedding Pipeline)

start

:**1. Problem Definition & Requirements**
----
* Define use case
  (Text Generation, Classification,
   Summarization, Translation)
* Identify input/output format
* Define success metrics
  (Perplexity, BLEU, ROUGE, Accuracy)
* Determine model size constraints
  (Parameters, Memory, Latency)
* Set quality requirements
* Define inference requirements;

:**2. Data Collection & Sourcing**
----
* Identify text data sources
  (Web Scraping, APIs, Databases,
   Public Datasets, Books, Articles)
* Collect domain-specific corpora
* Gather user-generated content
* Obtain licensed datasets
* Ensure data diversity
* Document data sources
* Check data rights/licensing;

:**3. Data Quality Assessment**
----
* Check for completeness
* Assess text quality
* Identify noise and errors
* Detect duplicate content
* Analyze language distribution
* Check for bias in data
* Validate data integrity
* Measure dataset size;

:**4. Text Preprocessing & Cleaning**
----
* Remove HTML/XML tags
* Strip special characters
* Handle URLs and emails
* Remove or normalize emojis
* Fix encoding issues (UTF-8)
* Remove excessive whitespace
* Handle newlines and tabs
* Normalize unicode characters
* Remove control characters;

:**5. Text Normalization**
----
* Convert to lowercase (if needed)
* Expand contractions (don't → do not)
* Handle abbreviations
* Normalize punctuation
* Handle numbers and dates
* Standardize formats
* Apply language-specific rules
* Preserve semantic meaning;

:**6. Text Filtering & Selection**
----
* Remove toxic content
* Filter spam and gibberish
* Apply length filters
  (Min/Max tokens)
* Remove duplicates/near-duplicates
* Filter by language
* Quality-based filtering
* Apply content policies
* Balance dataset;

:**7. Tokenization Strategy**
----
* Choose tokenization method:
  - Byte-Pair Encoding (BPE)
  - WordPiece
  - SentencePiece
  - Unigram Language Model
* Define vocabulary size
  (e.g., 30K, 50K, 100K tokens)
* Handle unknown tokens
* Configure special tokens
  ([PAD], [UNK], [CLS], [SEP],
   [MASK], [EOS], [BOS])
* Set tokenization parameters;

:**8. Vocabulary Building**
----
* Train tokenizer on corpus
* Build token vocabulary
* Assign token IDs
* Create token-to-ID mapping
* Create ID-to-token mapping
* Save vocabulary file
* Calculate token frequencies
* Handle rare tokens
* Set merge rules (for BPE);

:**9. Text Tokenization**
----
* Apply tokenizer to corpus
* Convert text to token sequences
* Handle out-of-vocabulary words
* Apply subword splitting
* Preserve special tokens
* Generate token statistics
* Validate tokenization
* Store tokenized data;

:**10. Sequence Processing**
----
* Determine sequence length
  (e.g., 512, 1024, 2048 tokens)
* Apply padding/truncation
* Create attention masks
* Generate position indices
* Handle document boundaries
* Create segment embeddings
* Apply sequence chunking
* Maintain context windows;

:**11. Token Embedding Initialization**
----
* Define embedding dimension
  (e.g., 256, 512, 768, 1024)
* Initialize embedding matrix
  (Vocabulary Size × Embedding Dim)
* Choose initialization method
  (Random, Xavier, He, Pre-trained)
* Create position embeddings
* Create segment embeddings
* Set embedding layer parameters
* Configure embedding dropout;

:**12. Dataset Preparation**
----
* Create training batches
* Shuffle data
* Split train/validation/test
  (e.g., 98%/1%/1%)
* Create data loaders
* Set batch size
* Apply dynamic padding
* Implement data sampling
* Create evaluation datasets
* Prepare prompt templates
  (for instruction tuning);

:**13. Model Architecture Selection**
----
* Choose architecture type:
  - Encoder-only (BERT-style)
  - Decoder-only (GPT-style)
  - Encoder-Decoder (T5-style)
* Define model size:
  - Number of layers
  - Hidden dimension
  - Number of attention heads
  - Feed-forward dimension
  - Total parameters
* Configure architecture details:
  - Attention mechanism
  - Activation functions
  - Layer normalization
  - Dropout rates;

:**14. Model Component Setup**
----
**Embedding Layer:**
* Token embeddings
* Position embeddings
* Segment embeddings (optional)
* Embedding dropout

**Transformer Blocks:**
* Multi-head self-attention
* Attention masking
* Layer normalization
* Feed-forward network
* Residual connections
* Dropout layers

**Output Layer:**
* Linear projection layer
* Vocabulary size output
* Softmax activation;

:**15. Training Configuration**
----
* Select loss function
  (Cross-Entropy Loss)
* Choose optimizer
  (Adam, AdamW, SGD)
* Set learning rate
  (e.g., 1e-4 to 5e-4)
* Configure learning rate schedule
  (Warmup, Cosine Decay, Linear)
* Set batch size & gradient accumulation
* Configure mixed precision (FP16/BF16)
* Set weight decay
* Configure gradient clipping
* Set number of epochs/steps;

:**16. Model Training**
----
* Initialize model weights
* Load training data batches
* Forward pass:
  - Input token IDs
  - Apply embeddings
  - Process through transformer layers
  - Generate logits
* Calculate loss
* Backward pass:
  - Compute gradients
  - Apply gradient clipping
  - Update weights via optimizer
* Log training metrics
  (Loss, Perplexity)
* Save checkpoints
* Monitor GPU/memory usage;

repeat
  :**17. Validation & Evaluation**
  ----
  * Run on validation set
  * Calculate validation loss
  * Compute perplexity
  * Evaluate on downstream tasks
  * Check for overfitting
  * Analyze sample generations
  * Compare with baseline
  * Track convergence metrics;

  if (Model Converged?) then (No)
    :**18. Hyperparameter Adjustment**
    ----
    * Adjust learning rate
    * Modify batch size
    * Change warmup steps
    * Tune dropout rates
    * Adjust gradient clipping
    * Modify architecture
      (layers, dimensions);
    
    :Continue Training;
  else (Yes)
  endif
repeat while (Training Complete?) is (No)
->Yes;

:**19. Final Model Evaluation**
----
* Test on held-out test set
* Calculate test perplexity
* Run task-specific metrics:
  - BLEU score (translation)
  - ROUGE score (summarization)
  - Accuracy (classification)
  - F1 score
* Perform human evaluation
* Test on edge cases
* Analyze failure modes
* Benchmark against baselines
* Document performance;

if (Performance\nAcceptable?) then (No)
  :Analyze Issues\nand Iterate;
  note right
    May need to revisit:
    - Data collection
    - Architecture design
    - Training configuration
  end note
  stop
else (Yes)
endif

:**20. Model Optimization**
----
* Apply quantization
  (INT8, INT4)
* Perform weight pruning
* Apply knowledge distillation
* Optimize inference graph
* Compile model (TorchScript, ONNX)
* Optimize for hardware
  (GPU, CPU, TPU)
* Reduce model size
* Improve latency;

:**21. Export & Serialization**
----
* Save model weights
* Save vocabulary file
* Save tokenizer config
* Export to standard format
  (HuggingFace, ONNX, TensorRT)
* Document model card
* Version model artifacts
* Package dependencies
* Create inference script;

:**22. Deployment Setup**
----
* Choose deployment platform
  (Cloud, On-premise, Edge)
* Containerize model (Docker)
* Set up API endpoint
  (REST, gRPC, WebSocket)
* Configure serving framework
  (TorchServe, TensorFlow Serving,
   FastAPI, vLLM)
* Implement batching
* Set up load balancing
* Configure auto-scaling
* Implement rate limiting;

:**23. Inference Pipeline**
----
**Input Processing:**
* Receive text input
* Apply preprocessing
* Tokenize input text
* Convert to token IDs
* Create attention mask
* Prepare input tensors

**Model Inference:**
* Load model to memory
* Run forward pass
* Generate token logits
* Apply sampling strategy
  (Greedy, Beam Search,
   Top-k, Top-p/Nucleus,
   Temperature Sampling)
* Generate output tokens

**Output Processing:**
* Decode token IDs to text
* Apply post-processing
* Format response
* Return to user;

:**24. Model Monitoring**
----
* Track inference metrics:
  - Latency (p50, p95, p99)
  - Throughput (requests/sec)
  - Error rates
  - Token generation rate
* Monitor resource usage:
  - GPU utilization
  - Memory consumption
  - CPU usage
* Log predictions
* Track input distribution
* Monitor output quality
* Detect anomalies
* Alert on degradation;

:**25. Performance Analysis**
----
* Analyze user feedback
* Review failure cases
* Detect input drift
* Measure task accuracy
* Identify edge cases
* Benchmark competitors
* Calculate business metrics
* Assess user satisfaction;

if (Performance\nDegraded?) then (Yes)
  :**26. Model Update Strategy**
  ----
  * Collect new data
  * Fine-tune on new data
  * Retrain if needed
  * Validate updated model
  * A/B test new version
  * Gradual rollout
  * Monitor impact;
  
  :Deploy Updated Model;
else (No)
  :Continue Service;
endif

stop

legend right
  |= **LLM Lifecycle Phases** |
  | **Phase 1: Planning** |
  | - Problem Definition |
  | **Phase 2: Data Preparation** |
  | - Collection & Sourcing |
  | - Quality Assessment |
  | - Preprocessing & Cleaning |
  | - Normalization |
  | - Filtering |
  | **Phase 3: Tokenization** |
  | - Strategy Selection |
  | - Vocabulary Building |
  | - Text Tokenization |
  | - Sequence Processing |
  | **Phase 4: Embeddings** |
  | - Embedding Initialization |
  | - Dataset Preparation |
  | **Phase 5: Model Development** |
  | - Architecture Selection |
  | - Component Setup |
  | - Training Configuration |
  | - Model Training |
  | - Validation & Tuning |
  | **Phase 6: Evaluation** |
  | - Final Evaluation |
  | - Model Optimization |
  | **Phase 7: Deployment** |
  | - Export & Serialization |
  | - Deployment Setup |
  | - Inference Pipeline |
  | **Phase 8: Operations** |
  | - Monitoring |
  | - Performance Analysis |
  | - Continuous Updates |
endlegend

note right
  **Key Components:**
  * Text → Tokens → IDs
  * Token Embeddings
  * Position Embeddings
  * Transformer Layers
  * Self-Attention Mechanism
  * Feed-Forward Networks
  * Layer Normalization
  * Residual Connections
  * Output Projection
  * Softmax → Probabilities
  
  **Critical Metrics:**
  * Perplexity (lower is better)
  * Loss (training/validation)
  * Generation Quality
  * Inference Latency
  * Throughput
end note

@enduml
